      "role": "user",
      "content": "but it doesn't feel like a judgment. it feels like a fact. like, if you break a mirror, you can glue it back together but it'll never be smooth again. the cracks are always there. i feel like the cracks are all that's left of me. how is anyone supposed to \"work through\" something that has changed who they are at the core?",
